y's high of 84\u00b0F was the 21st warmest November 13 high (tied) of 155 since 1872, the warmest since 2024.","t_yest":"November 13: warmer than 85% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>84\u00b0F</strong> was the 21st warmest November 13 high (tied) of 155 since 1872, the warmest since 2024. The normal high for the date is 81\u00b0F, and the record is 88\u00b0F (1936). The low of <strong>74\u00b0F</strong> was the 28th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 155 since 1872.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Key West's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Key West has set <strong>38 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 64 that chance alone would give, and <strong>65 record highs</strong>, close to the 64 that chance alone would give. The 1950s hold the most record highs of any decade (90). Key West's all-time high is 97\u00b0F, on July 19, 1880.","t_chg":"Key West has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 151 complete years: Key West's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.13\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.17), about +2.0\u00b0F since 1874. Key West's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.13\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.09 to +0.16), about +1.9\u00b0F since 1874.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 10 of 12 months. Highs rose in 10 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Key West's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.17 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 40.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 1969 (62.92 in); the driest, 1974 (19.99 in). Key West almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 7 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows"}}